                <pb facs="0162" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8744: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-13T19:00:00-04:00">July 13, 1937—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. Your 228, July 13, 6 p.m. and Nanking’s 275, July 13, 3 p.m. Department
                    feels it desirable that you remain where you are pending <pb facs="0163" n="156"
                        xml:id="pg156"/> further developments. If developments cause you to feel
                    that you should proceed to Nanking, please consult Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
